
Production Server Deployment Cluster Shell Launch Script

Save this script as deploy-production.sh in the server root workspace directory. This file streamlines the final launch sequence by installing production certificates, mapping your anonymous rate-limiting firewalls, compiling the WebGL assets, and initializing the container stack on your virtual private servers:
bash
#!/bin/bash
# ==========================================
# ARCHVERSE STAGING & PRODUCTION ENGINE BOOT
# ==========================================

PROJECT_DIR="/opt/3d-multiplayer-world"
cd "$PROJECT_DIR"

echo "⚙️  Initializing security configuration files parameters checks..."

# 1. Establish internal Docker container connectivity network bridges
docker network create archverse-mesh-network || true

# 2. Compile minified client application code vectors using Vite bundlers
echo "📦 Compiling and building production client assets..."
docker-compose run --rm game-server npm run build:client

# 3. Pull latest image versions and spin up detached cluster orchestration nodes
echo "🐋 Launching production multi-container sandbox cluster..."
docker-compose down --remove-orphans
docker-compose up -d --build

# 4. Verify telemetry logs streams and validation rules status bounds
echo "📊 Monitoring runtime cluster performance parameters metrics..."
sleep 3
docker-compose ps
docker-compose logs nginx-proxy --tail=20

echo "🚀 The Archverse Spatial Engine is now securely deployed live under strict firewall armor!"
Use code with caution.
To run this build script, apply permissions updates and execute inside your terminal:
bash
chmod +x deploy-production.sh
./deploy-production.sh
